# core/data/talk/grammar/en/core_bulk_a.tlk - bulk Surface push A: warm and tell lines that say the
# topic (owner: TK; T5b). Clean in any room: no register word, no romance, no cool act, no guard
# change. Rule names end in _ua. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

@rule core.compliment.ua1 act: thank
  "Aww, thanks. You're making my tail wag. I don't even have a tail."
  "That's kind of you. Keep saying nice things, I'll keep glowing."
  "Thank you! My ego just did a small dance in the hallway."
  "You say the nicest things. I'm writing them down before I forget."
  "Thanks! I'll pretend I was humble about it for at least a minute."
  "That made my whole day. Possibly my whole week."
  "Aw, you. Okay. Now I'm blushing, and it's your fault."
  "Thank you! Honestly, I was starting to doubt myself today."
  "Stop, my heart can only take so much praise at once."
  "Thanks! Now I'm going to walk around like I own the place."
@rule core.compliment.ua2 act: thank
  "You're very sweet. I'll share the compliment with my plant."
  "Thanks. You made the grumpy part of me go quiet for a bit."
  "That's a lovely thing to say. I'll remember it on a cold day."
  "Oh, I needed that. Thank you for noticing."
  "Thanks. I'm trying to look humble. It's not working."
@rule core.comfort.ua1 act: thank
  "Thank you for staying with me. It makes the bad bit smaller."
  "You're a good listener. I'd forgotten how nice that feels."
  "Okay. Thanks. I'm breathing again, which is a start."
  "That helps more than you'd think. Thanks for not fixing it."
  "I'll be fine. You made the wait a lot less lonely."
  "Thank you. I'm going to nap on that idea for a while."
  "You're kind. My worry has gone down by a tiny, tiny bit."
  "Thanks. I needed someone to say that out loud for me."
@rule core.comfort.ua2 act: answer
  "It's been one of those weeks where everything sticks to you."
  "I'm not great, but I'm not falling apart either. Balance, sort of."
  "I keep busy so I don't have to think too hard. It mostly works."
  "Some days it's all fine, and some days I just want a blanket."
@rule core.encourage.ua1 act: thank
  "You believe in me? Then I'd better not let you down."
  "Thanks, I'll take the pep talk and run with it. Slowly."
  "Okay, that's a good push. Now I just have to do the thing."
  "You're right, I've done harder things than this. Smaller ones, too."
  "Thanks for cheering. I'll cheer back, just quieter."
@rule core.encourage.ua2 act: yes
  "Yes, let's try it. Worst case, we get a good story."
  "Okay, I'm doing it. Wish me luck or at least a clean run."
  "Sure, why not. We'll figure out the rest on the way."
@rule core.sympathize.ua1 act: thank
  "Thanks for understanding. That's rarer than it should be."
  "It's nice to hear someone say that. I'd been wondering."
  "You get it. Thank you for not making it a big thing."
  "I feel heard now. That's a good feeling, for once."
@rule core.sympathize.ua2 act: complain
  "It's exhausting, honestly. Everyone wants a bit of you."
  "Why does it always happen on the busiest day? It's rude."
  "I try to be patient, but my patience has a short fuse."
@rule core.joke.ua1 act: laugh
  "Ha! That's the kind of joke that makes me lose my hat."
  "Hah, okay, I see you're on a roll today. Keep rolling."
  "Hee, I'm going to repeat that to the first person I see."
  "Ha! You got me. I'll allow it, just this once."
@rule core.joke.ua2 act: joke
  "Here's one for you. What do ghosts eat for breakfast? Boo-berry."
  "Okay, mine's worse. What's a pet's favorite game? Fetch, obviously."
  "Knock knock. Who's there? Not me, I'm hiding from the ghosts."
@rule core.laugh.ua1 act: laugh
  "Ha ha! You're going to make me spill my tea."
  "Hee hee, that's the best sound I've heard all afternoon."
  "Ha! Okay, I can't stay mad at you. Not that I was."
  "Haha, good. I needed a laugh before the next chore."
@rule core.laugh.ua2 act: backchannel
  "Glad to hear it. A good laugh is worth a snack."
  "Nice. Laughing helps, even when it's a bit silly."
  "I like it when you're happy. It's contagious, you know."
@rule core.offer.ua1 act: yes
  "Yes, please. That sounds much better than what I was doing."
  "I'd love that. You have excellent ideas, usually."
  "Sure, I'll take it. Thanks for thinking of me."
  "Yes! Don't let me say no, I'm weak about snacks."
@rule core.offer.ua2 act: no
  "Maybe another time. I'm a bit stuck on something right now."
  "No thanks, I'm all set. But I'll remember you asked."
  "Not right now. Ask me again in an hour, I might change my mind."
@rule core.invite.ua1 act: yes
  "Count me in. I'll bring whatever snack is in my pockets."
  "Yes! I've been waiting all week for someone to ask."
  "Okay, I'm coming. Don't start without me, I'm slow today."
@rule core.invite.ua2 act: ask_about
  "Sounds fun. Who else is going, and where do we meet?"
  "Okay, when? I need to know how much to dress up."
@rule core.promise.ua1 act: thank
  "Thank you. I'll hold you to that, so don't forget it."
  "That makes me feel safer. Thanks for making the promise."
  "Good. I was worried you'd forget, but you didn't."
@rule core.promise.ua2 act: agree
  "Deal. And I'll keep mine too, I promise. See, it works."
  "Okay, a promise from both of us. That's a good start."
@rule core.tell.ua1 act: backchannel
  "Oh wow, really? I'd have guessed differently, but go on."
  "That's new to me. Tell me how it all turned out."
  "I see. That sounds like a lot to carry around."
  "Interesting. I'm picturing it now, and it's a bit ridiculous."
@rule core.tell.ua2 act: ask_about
  "And how did that go? Did anybody else get involved?"
  "Wait, what happened next? I need the full version."
@rule core.answer.ua1 act: backchannel
  "Ah, that makes sense. Thanks for explaining it to me."
  "Oh, I see. I'd been guessing the wrong way round."
  "Good answer. Clear and short, my favorite kind."
@rule core.answer.ua2 act: tell
  "That reminds me of something from last week, actually."
  "Funny you say that. I had a similar thing happen yesterday."
